# The service's own env. Copy to `.env` and edit; `.env` is gitignored and
# `.env.example` is not (see the `!.env.example` line in `.gitignore` — without
# it, `.env*` swallows this file and `git add` says nothing while the tree has
# no example for anybody who clones).
#
# THE "SERVICE ENV" BLOCK, from `kit/templates/compose/.env.example`. The
# convention is fleet-wide and this file is this repository's copy of it, so a
# reader does not have to go looking in kit to learn the names.
#
#   OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=<repo name, lowercase>          e.g. parlor
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
#   OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio
#   OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=1.0
#   OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=deployment.environment=local,service.namespace=cafaye

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE TELEMETRY GOES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `PARLOR_OTEL_ENDPOINT` is the ONE variable
# `core/schemas/telemetry/otel-endpoint.schema.json` names as the contract, and
# it wins over the standard name below. Unset is NOT a no-op: the endpoint falls
# back to `http://otel-collector:4318`, which is the collector the local stack
# ships — "observability on by default without being mandatory". See
# HANDOFF-otel-01 §3, which is the open question on that.
# PARLOR_OTEL_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESOURCE ATTRIBUTES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read in `src/lib/telemetry.ts`'s `buildResource()`. `tenant_id` is a RESOURCE
# attribute and not a span attribute on purpose: per-tenant cardinality on a
# measurement overflows silently and undercounts while the total stays right.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=parlor
# DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT=local
# PARLOR_TENANT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SWITCHES THAT MAKE BOOT FREE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true` is the OTel spec's own kill switch and the mechanism
# core's schema pins the no-op to: no provider, no exporter, no queue, no dial,
# and one line in the log. The three `*_EXPORTER=none` switches are the finer
# half and ALL THREE are checked — a no-op that only covers traces is a service
# that still phones home for metrics, which is the failure a customer's invoice
# finds before a test does.
# OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true
# OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=none
# OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=none
# OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=none